Mirror upstream's EchoContainer image from the retired k8s.gcr.io registry to
our own GitLab Container Registry (registry.gitlab.com/haproxy-haptic/haptic/
ingress-conformance-echo:v0.0.1). The image content is identical — pinned by
the same SHA256 digest — but moves the source registry off the deprecated
k8s.gcr.io / registry.k8s.io chain, where pulls from GitLab.com SaaS runners
exceed the upstream suite's 5-minute WaitForEndpointsTimeout
(test/kubernetes/kubernetes.go) and cause a consistent first-scenario failure
in `Default_backend / no rules / should send all requests to the default
backend` (issue #45). Every subsequent scenario passed because by then the
image was cached in containerd; only the cold first pull blew the deadline.

The mirrored copy is populated and refreshed by the `mirror-ingress-
conformance-image` CI job, which runs on schedule + manually and pushes via
$CI_JOB_TOKEN. The job pins the same SHA256 digest as the upstream constant,
so a future upstream image bump requires updating both this patch and the
mirror job's source digest.

Apply with `git apply` from the upstream checkout root. Pinned to commit
d920ed36a0076e169a9a329a850844ab3a695ae8 — bumping that SHA in the Makefile
may require re-resolving this patch.

